From c8201140f4aafac7717c89cda4c155955c7dafc4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 06:07:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2260/2271] drm/bridge: synopsys: dw-dp: Signal BT.2020
 colorimetry for the output encoding

The "Colorspace" property documents BT2020_RGB and BT2020_YCC as
equivalent: the driver picks RGB or YCbCr output, and must then tell
the sink to expect BT.2020 R'G'B' or BT.2020 non-constant luminance
Y'C'bC'r respectively.

The VSC SDP colorimetry code is interpreted per pixel encoding, and
DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_RGB has the same value as
DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_CYCC. dw-dp copied the property value through,
so when it fell back to a YCbCr format (e.g. YCbCr 4:2:0 for 4K60 on a
link that cannot carry RGB) with Colorspace set to BT2020_RGB, it
announced constant luminance BT.2020 Y'cC'bcC'rc. A Samsung LU28R55
behind a DP to HDMI converter then showed a PQ test pattern with its
mid-grey levels crushed to black.

Pick the BT.2020 code from the output encoding, as the downstream
Rockchip driver does.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c | 14 +++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
index 50989fe0ac71..2ed9c78f7ed4 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
@@ -1270,10 +1270,18 @@ static int dw_dp_send_vsc_sdp(struct dw_dp *dp)
 
 	switch (state->colorspace) {
 	case DRM_MODE_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_RGB:
-		vsc.colorimetry = DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_RGB;
-		break;
 	case DRM_MODE_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_YCC:
-		vsc.colorimetry = DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_YCC;
+		/*
+		 * The two variants are equivalent: signal the one that matches
+		 * the output encoding. For a YCbCr pixel encoding the value of
+		 * DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_RGB means constant luminance
+		 * BT.2020 Y'cC'bcC'rc, not the non-constant luminance Y'C'bC'r
+		 * that is sent.
+		 */
+		if (state->color_format == DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB444)
+			vsc.colorimetry = DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_RGB;
+		else
+			vsc.colorimetry = DP_COLORIMETRY_BT2020_YCC;
 		break;
 	default:
 		if (state->color_format == DRM_OUTPUT_COLOR_FORMAT_RGB444)
-- 
